  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST find an ancestor containing both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`, require a nonempty relative mdBook source path without parent components and a `SUMMARY.md` at that path, and report an error when these prerequisites are absent or invalid.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.cli.setup_project`. The only weak spot is that the `habeas setup` \"no project found\" error is not tested directly.\n\n**Implementation (`src/setup.rs`)**\n- `find_project_root` walks `cwd.ancestors()` and returns the first directory that has both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml` as files.\n- `project_root` turns a `None` result into the error \"cannot find a project with Cargo.toml and book.toml\".\n- `book_source` defaults to `src` when `[book]` or `book.src` is absent. It reports an error if `book` is not a table or `book.src` is not a string.\n- `run` rejects an empty source. It also rejects any source path with a component that is not `Normal` or `CurDir`, so `..`, absolute paths and prefixes are refused. The error is \"book.src must be a directory inside this project\".\n- `run` then checks that `<source>/SUMMARY.md` is a file. If it isn't, it returns \"cannot find mdBook SUMMARY.md in …\".\n- All of these checks run before any file is written or `cargo add` is invoked.\n\n**Tests (`tests/setup.rs`)**\n- `setup_rejects_invalid_book_configuration` covers the invalid cases through the real binary:\n  - `book` not a table;\n  - `src` not a string;\n  - empty `src`;\n  - absolute `src`;\n  - `../outside`.\n\n  It also covers a missing `md/SUMMARY.md`. Each case asserts a nonzero exit status and the expected stderr message.\n- `setup_uses_src_when_book_table_or_source_setting_is_absent` covers the default `src` for an empty `book.toml` and for a `[book]` table without `src`. It then checks that a non-string `src` is treated as invalid.\n- `session_start_advises_only_when_setup_is_incomplete` exercises `find_project_root` through the hook:\n  - It finds the root from a nested cwd.\n  - Removing `book.toml` gives no project root.\n\n**Gaps**\n- No test runs `habeas setup` itself with no ancestor project. That path is a one-line `ok_or_else` over `find_project_root`, whose `None` case the hook test does cover.\n- No test runs `habeas setup` from a nested directory. The shared ancestor-search function is tested via the hook.\n\nI judge both gaps minor, so I am not choosing FIXME or false.",
